INT. PÂTISSERIE DU MATIN - BACK ROOM - PRE-DAWN

Flour on every surface. Cooling racks. A walk-in oven the size of a closet. In the corner, a three-tier wedding cake on a steel cart.

LEONID TARASOV, 40s, ski mask pushed up on his forehead, wedges a crowbar under the cake's base. CASPIAN ROWE, 30s, glasses, gloves, stands guard at the door with a cold coffee.

CASPIAN
Leo. It's a cake.

LEONID
It's a safe.

CASPIAN
It's a cake with a safe in it.

LEONID
Which makes it a safe.

He pries. The base creaks. A hidden panel pops. Inside: a small steel door, a keypad.

CASPIAN
Four digits.

LEONID
Try his birthday.

CASPIAN
He's seventy.

LEONID
Try it.

Caspian punches in numbers. Nothing. He tries again. A red light flashes. A tiny alarm warbles inside the cake.

They freeze. Leonid grabs the cake. Caspian grabs Leonid. They topple into the cart, tier two sliding off and splattering across the floor in a wet pink avalanche.

The alarm dies. Both men lie in frosting.

LEONID (CONT'D)
(whisper)
You did that.

CASPIAN
You pushed me!

LEONID
You grabbed me!

They scramble up, slipping. Leonid lunges for the keypad. Caspian shoves him aside, jabs at the buttons.

The light turns green. The little door swings open.

Inside: a single plastic bag, a scribbled note. Caspian reads it aloud.

CASPIAN (CONT'D)
"Nice try. -Mom."

They stare at each other. Frosting drips from both their chins.
